UID:f3871f9657fc0452@role-real-estate-title.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260930T221338Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260623
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Exxon Mobil Corp. v. Corporación Cimex\, S. 
 A. (Cuba)
DESCRIPTION:PRELIMINARY PRINT \nVolume 609 U. S. Part 1 \nPages 108–140 
 \nOFFICIAL REPORTS \nOF \nTHE SUPREME COURT \nJune 23\, 2026 \nREBECCA A. 
 WOMELDORF \nreporter of decisions \nPage Proof Pending Publication\nNOTICE
 : This preliminary print is subject to formal revision before \nthe bound 
 volume is published. Users are requested to notify the Reporter \nof Decis
 ions\, Supreme Court of the United States\, Washington\, D. C. 20543\, \np
 io@supremecourt.gov\, of any typographical or other formal errors. \nPage 
 Proof Pending Publication\n108 OCTOBER TERM\, 2025 \nSyllabus \nEXXON MOBI
 L CORP. v. CORPORACIÓN CIMEX\, S. A. \n(CUBA)\, et al. \ncertiorari to th
 e united states court of appeals for \nthe district of columbia circuit \n
 No. 24–699. Argued February 23\, 2026—Decided June 23\, 2026 \nIn 1960
 \, after Fidel Castro seized power in Cuba\, the Cuban Government \nconfsc
 ated many foreign-owned assets\, including Exxon's oil refnery\, \ntermina
 ls\, packaging plants\, and more than a hundred service stations. \nSince 
 then\, two Cuban government-owned companies—Unión Cuba-\nPetróleo (CUP
 ET) and Corporación CIMEX\, S. A. (Cuba) (CIMEX)— \nhave operated and p
 rofted from Exxon's expropriated assets. Exxon \nhad no good way to sue th
 e Cuban government entities and seek com-\npensation for its confscated pr
 operty until Congress passed and Presi-\ndent Clinton signed the Helms-Bur
 ton Act in 1996. As relevant here\, \nthe Act created a private right of a
 ction for U. S. nationals whose prop-\nerty was confscated by the Cuban Go
 vernment against “any person that \n. . . traffcs in” the confscated p
 roperty\, 22 U. S. C. § 6082(a)(1)(A)\, with \n“person” defned to inc
 lude “any agency or instrumentality of a foreign \nstate\,” § 6023(11
 ). Exxon sued CUPET\, CIMEX\, and later CIMEX's \nPanamanian alter ego und
 er the Helms-Burton Act in the U. S. District \nCourt for the District of 
 Columbia\, seeking more than $1 billion in dam-\nages. The Cuban governmen
 t-owned companies moved to dismiss\, as-\nserting immunity under the gener
 ally applicable Foreign Sovereign \nhttps://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/
 25pdf/609us1r56_3e04.pdf
URL:https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/25pdf/609us1r56_3e04.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:65cded7d60052cde@role-real-estate-title.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260930T221247Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] National PA Week - October 6 through 12
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, quality\, cost-effective\, and patient-centered he
 althcare is essential to the well-being and quality of life of all people 
 in Maine\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, physician associates/assistants (PAs) are nati
 onally certified and state-licensed medical professionals who diagnose ill
 nesses\, develop and manage treatment plans\, prescribe medications\, and 
 often serve as a patient's principal healthcare provider\; and\nWHEREAS\n\
 , PAs are trusted providers and vital members of the healthcare team\, enh
 ancing access to high-quality care in primary care settings\, hospitals\, 
 rural communities\, and underserved areas\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, PAs deliver c
 ompassionate\, expert care\, often serving as the first point of contact f
 or patients and empowering individuals and families to be active participa
 nts in their own health\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, PAs provide critical care acros
 s a broad range of medical specialties\, including addressing the growing 
 demand for behavioral and mental health services by offering compassionate
 \, evidence-based care to individuals and families in need\; and\nWHEREAS\
 n\, PAs are committed to addressing health disparities\, expanding access\
 , and providing team-based\, person-centered care across every medical spe
 cialty and setting\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, PAs have earned the respect of patie
 nts and colleagues alike for their clinical excellence\, adaptability\, an
 d deep dedication to the communities they serve\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine h
 as been a leader in progressing PA practice and ensuring access to PA serv
 ices by enacting legislation in recent years to join the PA compact\, chan
 ge the title of the profession to accurately reflect the scope of the prof
 ession\, and allow PAs to practice at the top of their education and train
 ing\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Govern
 or of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim October 6-12\, 2026 as\nNati
 onal PA Week\nin Maine\, and I encourage all residents to recognize and ce
 lebrate the important role that PAs play in improving health\, advancing e
 qui\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/
 2026-09-national-pa-week-october-6-through-12
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-national-pa-week-october-6-through-12
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
